      "math_academy_id": "q-32519",
      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "Calculate ${\\int }_{0}^{1}[f(t)-g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t$ given that ${\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨\\frac{1}{2},\\,2,\\,1⟩$ and ${\\int }_{0}^{1}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨1,\\,1,\\,1⟩.$",
      "worked_solution": "From the vector addition rule, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1}[f(t)-g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{0}^{1}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[f(t)-g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{0}^{1}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2},\\,2,\\,1⟩-⟨1,\\,1,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{2},\\,1,\\,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
